  "id": "speaking/what-the-agent-has-in-mind-makes-the-classifier-policy-offer-at-its-proactivity",
  "title": "With a thought, the classifier policy also judges whether what the agent wants to say answers or corrects the turn: not addressed, the agent offers when that reaches the proactivity, half of it for an urgent thought, never on urgency alone; only wondered about and knowing the answer, it speaks",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4",
    "§6.8"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.4-201",
    "RK-6.4-202"
  ],
  "notes": "Each room holds one turn of Bob's to Alice: first decided without a thought, silent, it is thought about, and the thought comes back in time with something to say, so the policy is asked again with it and is asked too whether it answers or corrects the turn and whether a question waits for someone else. The proactivity is the default, 0.5. Each room's thought is its own (urgent in r3 and r4). RK-6.4-201 is cited in part: what makes a question still open, or still waiting for someone's first try, is the classifier's judgment over the state it reads. Python: speaking/classifier.py compose, THOUGHT_QUESTIONS.",
